Never waiting for the web process to paint (Kosmos testing.md 18.860).
Painting a page with no backing store yet - while it loads, or a tab just
opened - forced an update and waited up to half a second for it, the
window frozen, and a loading page's process is busy: on the M700 one paint
in four took 500 ms when Wikipedia was opened. The area is left unpainted
instead, and the picture comes when it comes. And a visible page's store,
which the screen shows (patch 0044), is not discarded ten seconds after
the window last painted it.

diff -ru a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/CoordinatedGraphics/DrawingAreaProxyCoordinatedGraphics.cpp b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/CoordinatedGraphics/DrawingAreaProxyCoordinatedGraphics.cpp
--- a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/CoordinatedGraphics/DrawingAreaProxyCoordinatedGraphics.cpp	2026-11-17 17:03:51.429537340 -0300
+++ b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/CoordinatedGraphics/DrawingAreaProxyCoordinatedGraphics.cpp	2026-11-17 17:03:51.446350974 -0300
@@ -83,8 +83,21 @@
     if (isInAcceleratedCompositingMode())
         return;
 
+#if PLATFORM(KOSMOS)
+    // **Never waiting for the web process to paint** (Kosmos testing.md
+    // 18.860). Without a backing store yet - a page still loading, a tab
+    // just opened - `forceUpdateIfNeeded` asked the web process for a
+    // picture and waited up to half a second for it, the window frozen,
+    // and a page loading is exactly when its process is busy. The area is
+    // left unpainted (the caller fills it with the page's background), and
+    // the picture comes when the web process has one, as every picture
+    // does.
+    if (!m_backingStore)
+        return;
+#else
     if (!m_backingStore && !forceUpdateIfNeeded())
         return;
+#endif
 
     m_backingStore->paint(cr, rect);
     unpaintedRegion.subtract(IntRect(IntPoint(), m_backingStore->size()));
@@ -333,6 +346,14 @@
 {
     if (!m_backingStore)
         return;
+#if PLATFORM(KOSMOS)
+    // A visible page's store is what the screen shows (patch 0044), and
+    // throwing it away ten seconds after the window last painted it, as
+    // other ports do, only makes the web process paint the whole view
+    // again into a new one (Kosmos testing.md 18.860).
+    if (RefPtr page = this->page(); page && page->isViewVisible())
+        return;
+#endif
 
     m_backingStore = nullptr;
     send(Messages::DrawingArea::DidDiscardBackingStore());
